<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e2d1a0a6">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The amount and specificity of information included in this work product varies from project to project depending on
        various factors such as project needs, confidentiality.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Some organizations may have an established procurement process for engaging suppliers. Consult with stakeholders to
        verify any existing procurement guidelines to follow.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        In some cases, EY involvement in Request for Proposal documentation may be limited to assisting stakeholders
        develop questions to be answered. In others, EY involvement may be asked to help develop company and project
        overview sections as well as response instructions for suppliers to follow.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;
    Independence Considerations
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For engagements with Channel 1 clients, EY can advise, review and provide observations on management’s package
    selection. EY cannot draft or develop the request, nor administer the package selection process on the
    client&apos;s behalf.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    For engagements with Channel 2 clients, EY can assist management in the development of a package selection, subject to
    management review and approval.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Although generally permitted for Channel 2 engagements, EY cannot interact directly with a supplier who is an audit
    client if EY is involved in assisting the client with the package selection process, other than very limited
    interaction related to information gathering.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="3223730f"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="15a951df"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="59cf3bac">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product contains stakeholder devised prompts for suppliers to describe their skills, experience and solution
    capabilities. In addition, this work product also includes contextual and instructional information to facilitate
    supplier responses. Contextual and instructional information provides suppliers with the appropriate perspective to
    answer stakeholders questions. Questions posed in a Request For Proposal are typically more detailed than those in
    Request For Information submissions. Information suppliers are typically asked to provide include, but is not limited
    to, the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Functional and technical capabilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Support capabilities
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Implementation planning
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Pricing information
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        References
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
